---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Conduct & etiquette" description="The First & Last Pickleball Club conduct and etiquette policy — dress code, line calls, respect on court, and how to raise a concern.">
  <section>
    <div class="container narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow">How we play</p>
      <h1>Conduct &amp; etiquette.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        The purpose of the club is the enjoyment of pickleball. That implies proper etiquette and
        sportsmanship from every player — what follows is the policy all members are asked to
        observe.
      </p>

      <h2>Dress code</h2>
      <p>
        We like to keep things relaxed at the club, but a few simple standards help everyone feel
        comfortable on court. Please wear suitable sportswear and non-marking trainers, and keep
        tops on while playing — it helps maintain the friendly, welcoming atmosphere we're known
        for. Otherwise, comfort is key: dress for the weather, bring a layer or two when it's cold,
        and wear whatever lets you move and enjoy your game.
      </p>
      <p>
        Thanks for helping keep First &amp; Last a great place to play for members of all ages and
        abilities.
      </p>

      <h2>Before and after each game</h2>
      <ul class="bullets">
        <li>Give your opponent time to get into position before you serve.</li>
        <li>
          The server must call the score before they serve. If you're unsure of the score, ask the
          other players — the receiving side or non-server must correct the call if it's wrong.
        </li>
        <li>
          Introduce yourself to any players you don't know at the start of a game, and thank your
          opponents at the end.
        </li>
        <li>
          Welcome new members and be prepared to help explain the rules and offer guidance as
          needed.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Line calls and foot faults</h2>
      <ul class="bullets">
        <li>
          Make quick and fair line calls and accept those made by your opponents on their half. If
          there's any uncertainty, the ball is considered <em>in</em>. If you're some distance from
          the ball, remember that parallax can be a factor — call <em>in</em> unless clearly out by
          some margin.
        </li>
        <li>
          Try not to question a line call or foot fault — accept the call gracefully. If you do feel
          you need to challenge, do it once only and in a friendly way. Don't make disrespectful
          comments, argue, or accuse the other team of dishonesty. If you feel specific players
          regularly make dubious line calls, speak to the committee privately and we'll deal with
          the matter accordingly.
        </li>
        <li>
          A fault will be called if you or your partner steps into the non-volley zone on a volley,
          or steps in (by momentum) after playing a shot from outside it. Accept other players
          identifying foot faults on your side — and be the kind of player who identifies and
          accepts their own.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Respect</h2>
      <ul class="bullets">
        <li>
          Bullying, verbal abuse, threatening behaviour and shouting will not be tolerated. Anyone
          breaking this policy may be removed from the club.
        </li>
        <li>Refrain from swearing at club sessions, particularly while playing.</li>
        <li>Always be supportive of your partner and respect your opponents.</li>
        <li>
          Respect F&amp;L Pickleball Club and GO! St Just's property — perform no actions which may
          cause damage.
        </li>
        <li>
          Behave in a manner consistent with the F&amp;L constitution, and endeavour to be an
          ambassador for the sport.
        </li>
        <li>
          If your opponent claims a major distraction during a point (e.g. a ball bouncing onto the
          court), don't hesitate to replay it.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Targeting and body shots</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Targeting</strong> — deliberately playing most balls to one player throughout the
        match — is not allowed at club sessions. It exists to make sure all four players are
        involved. The same goes for <strong>body shots</strong>: deliberately hard hits at a person
        are not allowed. Both are permitted only in sessions described as "tournament play".
      </p>

      <h2>Dangerous play</h2>
      <p>Dangerous play is not allowed at club nights. This includes:</p>
      <ul class="bullets">
        <li>
          Hitting the ball towards someone with such power that, if it caught them, it would injure
          them — particularly above waist height. (Hitting hard into a large space or at someone's
          feet is acceptable.)
        </li>
        <li>
          Hitting the ball hard without the necessary control. If you can't be sure where it will
          go, hit it more gently.
        </li>
        <li>Not moving away when someone else calls for the ball — you could be hit by their paddle.</li>
        <li>Crashing into the net.</li>
        <li>Not stopping play when a ball is on court.</li>
        <li>
          Running onto an adjoining court when play is in action there. If this happens, play a let.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Attendance</h2>
      <p>
        If you know you won't be able to attend club night for more than two weeks — injury,
        illness, work changes, holidays — please let the group know on Spond so we can plan court
        numbers.
      </p>

      <h2>Junior players</h2>
      <p>
        Sunday sessions are open to ages 10 and up. Improvers sessions are 16+; Wednesday's
        Intermediate Plus is 18+. When juniors are on court, the standard expected of adult
        behaviour, language and attitude is higher, not lower. Safeguarding concerns should be
        raised with the committee immediately — see below.
      </p>

      <h2>Raising concerns</h2>
      <p>
        Members are asked to direct all club business — comments on policy, issues, suggestions
        and any concerns — to
        <a href="mailto:firstandlastpickleballuk@yahoo.com">firstandlastpickleballuk@yahoo.com</a>.
        Anything you tell us in confidence will be treated as such.
      </p>

      <p class="footer-note">Conduct &amp; etiquette policy — adopted August 2023.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .narrow { max-width: 46rem; }
  h2 {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    padding-top: 1rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  h2:first-of-type { border-top: none; padding-top: 0; }
  .bullets {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 1rem 0;
  }
  .bullets li {
    padding: 0.55rem 0 0.55rem 1.5rem;
    position: relative;
    border-bottom: 1px dashed var(--line);
  }
  .bullets li:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
  .bullets li::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 1.05rem;
    width: 6px;
    height: 6px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--coral);
  }
  .footer-note {
    margin-top: 3rem;
    padding-top: 1.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    color: var(--sea-light);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    font-style: italic;
  }
</style>
